======================================================================================
LABEL-LEAKAGE CHECK
======================================================================================
ADNI assigns diagnostic group using cognitive testing. A variable that reproduces the stage almost perfectly is not an independent predictor -- it is the label in another form.

variable                   n     Spearman rho         p  reading
age (Age_years)           94           -0.002  9.88e-01  weak association
APOE4 (APOE4_allele_co   113           +0.350  1.46e-04  weak association
MMSE (MMSE_total)         94           -0.563  3.36e-09  moderate association
CDR-SB (CDR_SB)           94           +0.846  7.52e-27  SEVERE LEAKAGE RISK
hypertension (MH4CARD_    94           -0.025  8.09e-01  weak association
diabetes (MH9ENDO_clea    94           +0.147  1.58e-01  weak association
GDS (GDS_total)           94           +0.230  2.56e-02  weak association


Interpretation:
  CDR-SB (rho = +0.85) is a component of the diagnostic criteria themselves -- it is the label in another form and MUST NOT be a model input.
  MMSE (rho = -0.56) is also used in staging and carries the same risk to a lesser degree.
  APOE4 (rho = +0.35) is a genuine genetic risk factor, not part of the staging decision, and its association is of the magnitude the literature would lead one to expect. It is a defensible input.
  Age, cardiovascular history and endocrine history show NO useful association with stage in this cohort (|rho| <= 0.15), so they are safe but probably uninformative.

